From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: videobuf2-dma-contig: Drop NO_KERNEL_MAPPING on non-coherent alloc

dma_alloc_noncontiguous() takes no attribute but
DMA_ATTR_ALLOC_SINGLE_PAGES and warns and fails on any other. A queue
that sets DMA_ATTR_NO_KERNEL_MAPPING and allows cache hints, as the
rkvdec and Hantro decoders' capture queues do, therefore cannot
allocate a single buffer once userspace asks for non-coherent memory.
A non-coherent buffer is never mapped into the kernel at allocation
anyway, only in vb2_dc_vaddr() on demand, so drop the attribute there.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/common/videobuf2/videobuf2-dma-contig.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/common/videobuf2/videobuf2-dma-contig.c b/drivers/media/common/videobuf2/videobuf2-dma-contig.c
index 9ce6284..e4ddb4b 100644
--- a/drivers/media/common/videobuf2/videobuf2-dma-contig.c
+++ b/drivers/media/common/videobuf2/videobuf2-dma-contig.c
@@ -215,7 +215,8 @@ static int vb2_dc_alloc_non_coherent(struct vb2_dc_buf *buf)
 					       buf->size,
 					       buf->dma_dir,
 					       GFP_KERNEL | q->gfp_flags,
-					       buf->attrs);
+					       buf->attrs &
+					       ~DMA_ATTR_NO_KERNEL_MAPPING);
 	if (!buf->dma_sgt)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
